@startuml mcp-tool-call
' Sequence: LLM agent -> MCP server (JSON-RPC over stdio) -> a tool ->
' AlertCenter / historian -> JSON response.
'
' Grounded in real source:
'   - src/mcp/McpServer.h/.cpp  (run(istream,ostream): getline -> json::parse
'     -> route on method -> writeResponse; ctor holds alerts/reader/production/
'     presenter/session/writeEnabled)
'   - src/mcp/McpProtocol.h  (kJsonRpcVersion="2.0"; methods initialize,
'     tools/list, tools/call; handleInitialize/handleToolsList/handleToolsCall;
'     handleToolsCall routes on params["name"], forwards params["arguments"])
'   - src/mcp/tools/AlarmsSnapshotTool.h  (kAlarmsSnapshotTool="alarms_snapshot",
'     runAlarmsSnapshot(AlertCenter&) -> wraps AlertCenter::snapshot())
'   - src/mcp/tools/HistorianQueryTool.h  (kHistorianQueryTool="historian_query")
'   - src/mcp/tools/ProductionMetricsTool.h ("production_metrics")
'   - src/presenter/AlertCenter.h (snapshot()); src/historian/HistoryReader.h (query())

title MCP tool call - JSON-RPC over stdio -> read-only tool -> JSON result

skinparam shadowing false

participant "LLM agent\n(MCP client)" as Agent
participant "McpServer\n::run(stdin, stdout)" as Server
participant "McpProtocol\n::handleToolsCall" as Proto
participant "alarms_snapshot /\nhistorian_query tool" as Tool
participant "AlertCenter /\nHistoryReader" as Backend

== handshake ==
Agent -> Server : {"method":"initialize"}  (stdin line)
Server -> Server : handleInitialize(params)
Server --> Agent : result: protocolVersion + serverInfo\n(stdout line)
Agent -> Server : {"method":"tools/list"}
Server -> Server : handleToolsList(writeEnabled)
Server --> Agent : tool descriptors\n(equipment_command only if writeEnabled)

== tool call ==
Agent -> Server : {"method":"tools/call",\n"params":{"name":"alarms_snapshot"}}
Server -> Server : json::parse(line); method == "tools/call"
Server -> Proto : handleToolsCall(params, alerts, reader, ...)
Proto -> Proto : route on params["name"]
Proto -> Tool : runAlarmsSnapshot(alerts)\n(or historian_query -> reader.query())
Tool -> Backend : AlertCenter::snapshot()\n(or HistoryReader::query(range))
Backend --> Tool : active alarms / HistoryRecords
Tool --> Proto : nlohmann::json content
Proto --> Server : Result<json, McpErrorCode>
Server -> Server : successEnvelope(id, result)
Server --> Agent : JSON-RPC response line (stdout)

note over Server
  Single-threaded, synchronous: one request fully
  handled before the next getline. stdout IS the
  protocol channel (real logging goes to stderr).
  Unknown tool -> MethodNotFound; equipment_command
  when writeEnabled==false is neither listed nor callable.
end note

@enduml
